--   Fourth recurrence: exact shared integer values leadingSquare
-- statement:
--   A fixed integer coefficient list for one shared fourth-recurrence intermediate polynomial. The list is written in bounded literal chunks, so it can be reused in independently verified scalar identities. These definitions introduce no axiom and assume no torsion conclusion.
-- source:
--   User MazurTheorem WIP 54d43d8dda8a6fcf069cc02a815f850d762c5c0c, Apache-2.0. Candidate numbers were computed from actual typed pure integer expressions by tooling only. All five intermediate lists have separate closed ordinary Lean kernel equality proofs against their original total integer-list operations. This pure data package merely gives the fixed values; it imports no evaluator, protocol stub or proof oracle. Literal chunks contain at most sixteen integers and all exact list values are preserved. Named downstream consumers: the complete unchanged fourth-recurrence scalar identities, original recurrence4 and full every-curve order49 exclusion.

/- Apache-2.0. Pure candidate integer data; the separate closed anchor proves its exact value. -/
